# Logistics module map

**Acceptance SSOT:** [Logistics-Acceptance-System](../../../docs/acceptance/Logistics-Acceptance-System.md) · [Product-Readiness](../../../docs/acceptance/Logistics-Product-Readiness-Matrix.md) · edition [`docs/editions/logistics.yaml`](../../../docs/editions/logistics.yaml)

| Domain | API prefix | Notes |
|--------|------------|-------|
| Auth / SSO | `app/api/auth/` | local + SSO |
| Trips / waybill | `app/api/trips/` | points, POD, fuel, complete |
| Driver | `app/api/driver/` | driver trip list |
| Hub / scan | `app/api/hub/scan` | warehouse scan |
| Tracking | `app/api/tracking/` | staff session, then the path token selects the trip |
| COD | `app/api/cod/settle` | cash on delivery |
| Fleet | `app/api/fleet/alerts` | alerts |
| Reports | `app/api/reports/fuel` | fuel reporting |
| Events | `events/dispatch` | orchestrator |
| Internal | `GET/POST /api/internal/v1/organization/bind`, `GET/POST /api/internal/v1/runtime-config` | Orch Sync bind + desired-state config; `instrumentation` boot |

**Tenancy (CP-TENANT-01):** `organizationId` on tenant/ops models + kit Prisma extension + `requireSatelliteModule("industry_logistics")` (AC-LOG-TENANT 🟡 — not live SHARED pool).

| Access matrix (LOG-RBAC-01) | `app/api/admin/roles`, `admin/roles/[code]`, `admin/roles/[code]/permissions`, `api/internal/v1/workforce/roles`, `admin/users`, `auth/me`, `auth/session/refresh-permissions`, `auth/logout`; page `/admin/access` | `Role` (`isSystem`, `cloneFromCode`, `permissionCatalogVersion`), `SatelliteAuditLog`; catalog `src/lib/auth/permissions.ts`; page map `page-route-permissions.ts`; API map `api-route-permissions.ts` |

**RBAC Variant A (LOG-RBAC-01):** `getSatelliteSession()` also builds `permissions` from the role row and checks the stamped API path against `api-route-permissions.ts` (unlisted → 403). Pages: middleware `authorizePage` + `page-route-permissions.ts`. A new staff route or page needs a catalog row in the same change. `/api/driver/trips` is `api:driver.trips` on both ops packages; `/api/tracking/[token]` is session-only (any staff session, then the path token). A missing `x-era-pathname` denies. `POST /api/auth/logout` clears the staff cookie. ADR logistics-domain-permissions-and-rbac.
